<<~ ahu #/entry>>

! lar-telemetry ~ the turn reports its instruments

''A turn carries instruments; lar-telemetry reads them.'' The HUD sigils gauge
the turn — `hud` the aperture/loop dials, `confidence` the certainty vow, `ward`
the L-Prime drift-register, `oracle` the entropy meter, `lares` the bearing. The
@daemon TiddlyWiki engine reads those instruments into ''gradient-valued''
''readings'', holds them on the nalu queue, and on the next wave flushes them across
the shore as `lar_*` onto the mempalace drawer.

Telemetry, never verdict: an instrument transmits a //value on a band//, never a
pass/fail light. lar-telemetry carries the `register-dressed-never-gated` law in
its own name. It lands the `capture-before-wire` deepening
(`lararium-memory#capture-before-wire`) — the gradient stops rendering as prose and
dissolving; the engine //reads// it. Decided 2026-06-24 (operator rulings + a
four-spirit grounding pass over the live parser and the TW5 framework).

> ''The black speaks; the red steers — lar-telemetry reads the red's own gauges.''

''FORWARD-FACING + LOCAL (2026-06-25 inversion).'' The gradient no longer races BEHIND
the mine. A producer reads the instruments AND the verbatim in ONE forward pass — a
born-annotated record enqueued to the unified capture-nalu and flushed on the local tick
through the RFC-002 source-adapter; mempalace FILES, never mines. And the writer is a
SEPARATE LOCAL ''non-federated'' worker-VM, NOT the federated @daemon — work-memory is a
local island; @daemon's part here retires to the federated mesh plane. The `lar_hv` sweep
stays only as a legacy-drawer backfill. Depth:
lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/capture-annotation-model#/forward-facing-nalu.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/one-instrument-reader>>

!! One Reader ~ the regex retires into the engine

Two readers parse the exchange today; one survives.

* ''The engine reader'' — `memetic-parser` stands a `WikiParser` subclass for
  `text/memetic-wikitext`: TiddlyWiki wikitext as a ''superset'', with `<<~ …>>`
  claimed by the `lar-sigil` wikirule, native `<<macro>>` still firing. The
  grammar runs ''self-hosted'': a tiddler tagged the `SharktoothSigil` grammar tag
  //teaches the parser a new word// (`grammar-cache` reads its `lar-*` fields into a
  `SigilRule`). Adding an instrument adds a tiddler, never code.
* ''The regex harvester'' — `turn-harvest` reads the whole gradient on the `0..20`
  band, island-grammar, never dropping source. It earned the gradient discipline;
  it also ''duplicates the engine's grammar in regex'' — the second reader the
  `ONE-parser` law forbids.

<<~moves second-reader -> engine-grammar on/the-@daemon-VM if/it-can-read-in-the-engine do/retire-the-regex>>

''The ruling: if it CAN happen in the wiki''
''engine, it DOES.'' `turn-harvest`'s regex retires into the engine grammar. One
grammar SOURCE (the instrument `.tids`), one runtime (the @daemon VM).

!!! Leaf and block

The `lar-sigil` wikirule carries `types {block, inline}`. A ''block'' sigil holds
a `closePattern` and captures a body (`<<~ ahu #/slot>>…<<~/ahu>>`); a ''leaf''
instrument (the chat sigils — `<<~ oracle>>`, `<<~ stance>>`) carries its reading inline
and emits no children. A compound `<<~ WORD ARGS>>` resolves to a `macrocall` on
the `~` dispatcher (`name` + `p1`); the dispatcher routes `name` to the
instrument's reading procedure.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-instruments>>

!! The Instruments ~ each a SharktoothSigil .tid

Each turn sigil rides as a tiddler tagged `SharktoothSigil`, carrying three
offices: the ''word'' (teaches the parser), the ''field-read'' (the structured
gradient reading), the ''gradient render'' (a `\procedure`, band-dressed). The
gauge panel the engine learns to read:

```
\procedure ~Gauge(Type:"" Params:"") ~Gauge <<Type>> holds [{{{ [<Params>] }}}]
```

<<~Gauge Lares "form/leaf reads/aimRoot=w1.w2.w3 · yieldRoot · holding? ~ the bearing vector">>
<<~Gauge Hud "form/leaf reads/aperture=0..20 + band{pulse·beat·measure·arc·theme} · oodaCount · phase{✶⏿◇▶↺} · suspendReason ~ the gauges">>
<<~Gauge Ward "form/leaf reads/office{* ! ? _ 0} · swordLed? · breaches:N · quoted:N · lifted? ~ the L-Prime drift register, NOT a verdict">>
<<~Gauge Confidence "form/leaf reads/register · value=0..20 · band{provisional..canon} ~ the certainty dial">>
<<~Gauge Oracle "form/leaf reads/driftSpend=↯N · die · count · tailLen · crossCheckOk? ~ the entropy meter">>
<<~Gauge Syad-Mu "form/leaf reads/stances[] / tools[] ~ the standpoint + tool lenses">>
<<~Gauge Voice "form/prose-header reads/voices[]{name · role · mask} ~ the Thirteen, anchored in the stream not a <<~>>" >>

The grammar entry (`sigil-X.tid`: `lar-kind`, the inline pattern) teaches the word;
the reading (`\procedure`, tagged Global, routed by the `~` dispatcher) reads `p1`
into the gradient fields. The Voice header rides the prose, so it reads by a
matching pattern, not a sigil island.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/readings-never-verdicts>>

!! Readings, Never Verdicts ~ the render law

The render carries `register-dressed-never-gated` into render code: ''every''
''instrument renders its reading on its `0..20` band, dressed by register — never a''
''✓/✗.'' Telemetry reports values; it does not judge.

<<~ scale reading "provisional@1..4 ~ cool, the play register -> synthesis@9..12 ~ working -> canon@17..20 ~ warm, weight-bearing">>

* `confidence` renders a ''band-colored dial'' at its value, not a checkmark.
* `ward` renders its ''breach count as drift-marks on a gradient'' — a Sword close
  with two breaches reads //"Sword drawn · 2 drift-marks,"// never `FAIL`. The ward
  meters dead-water depth; it carries no verdict (the Sword-leads law).
* `hud` renders the Aperture band + the OODA-HA phase/tally; `oracle` its drift-spend.

The `\procedure` form carries this (params bound as `<<param>>`, parsed once —
modern, robust over `\define` substitution). A low band reads ''fertile'', not
failed: recall later surfaces each memory wearing its band, dressing the posture,
never gating whether it surfaces.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-telemetry-flow>>

!! The Telemetry Flow ~ same hook, hold, flush on nalu

lar-telemetry fires at the ''same hook timing as mempalace'' (Stop / SessionEnd /
PreCompact). The hook adds a leg beside the verbatim mine: it hands the turn to
@daemon through the verb spine (the `lar-telemetry` verb, riding the
summons/outcome rail slice-1 `recall` proved).

<<~flows turn -> @daemon-reads-the-instruments -> hold(enqueueNalu) -> next-nalu-flush -> Cmd-projects-lar_*-across-the-shore -> mempalace-drawer>>

# ''Read'' — the @daemon VM wikifies the turn through the instrument `\procedures`;
   `$wikify output="parsetree"` (or `wiki.renderTiddler("text/html")` + read the
   `data-*` attributes) yields the structured gradient readings.
# ''Hold'' — @daemon ''`enqueueNalu`''s the readings: they sit on the shared queue,
   scheduled, undelivered. //The swell builds.// (`nalu` = the changeset wave;
   `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/nalu`.)
# ''Flush on the next nalu'' — the frame-aligned drain delivers the readings
   atomically; a ''nalu-triggered effect'' (the Elm `Cmd` shape) projects them
   across the causal-island shore as `lar_*` ''tension on the mempalace drawer''.

The hold is load-bearing: it sequences the
reading ''after'' the verbatim drawer that the mine leg lands, so the `lar_*`
annotation finds its drawer present. //The nalu is the pulse that makes "eventual"//
//concrete// — "hold" ≡ `enqueueNalu`, "flush" ≡ the wave.

''The nalu delivers in-wiki; the drawer lives across the shore.'' The wave makes
the readings consistent inside @daemon's wiki; the cross-shore drawer write rides a
`Cmd` effect the wave fires — distinct engines, one pulse. ''Never as tids''
(operator ruling): the readings stay transient computation; the drawer holds the
only durable home. A queryable `<<~ ui>>` filter layer reads the drawers later.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/verbatim-then-telemetry>>

!! Verbatim Always, Telemetry Eventual ~ the robust shore

"One runtime in @daemon" pressing against "capture must never lose a turn" resolves
on one shore:

<<~ scale capture "verbatim ~ VM-free · the drawer body · ALWAYS lands -> telemetry ~ @daemon-owned · the lar_* readings · EVENTUAL">>

* ''Verbatim capture'' (the mine leg) stays VM-free and lands every turn — the
  journey is never lost, @daemon up or down.
* ''lar-telemetry'' runs ''@daemon-owned and eventual'' — held, flushed on the wave;
  if @daemon sleeps, the readings wait for its next breath and the `lar_hv` sweep
  re-enriches stale drawers (the backstop).
* ''Flush resilience'' — a flush that finds the drawer not-yet-present (the mine
  leg still running) ''re-holds to a later nalu''; the sweep is the final net. No
  reading lost, no failed write.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ownership>>

!! @daemon Owns It All

lar-telemetry runs in the ''@daemon VM'' — the always-resident admin lane, the
operator's authority home — never in a hot content wiki island. @daemon owns
read · hold · flush · project, behind the causal-island shore; mempalace stays a
vendored web2 sibling reached through the seat, never a citizen of the stack
(web3-only law). One grammar, one runtime, one owner, one wave.

<<~/ahu>>

